o"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about injuries.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to be laid up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be unable to move due to injury", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Aunt Nelly was laid up for weeks.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le03ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Hooray! ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "used to express joy and excitement", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Hooray! A strike!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le03ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to get injured", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to hurt yourself physically", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Someone always gets injured.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le03ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to lean", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to balance one's weight on someone or something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Lean on me and I'll lean on you.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le03ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "shooting pain", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a pain that is intense", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: I have a shooting pain going up my leg.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le03ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Second Conditional - Talking About Hypothetical Situations", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use the second conditional to talk about unreal or imaginary (hypothetical) situations in the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">If I had a million dollars, I would buy a car</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Do you have a million dollars?  No.<br/> Is it possible to suddenly get a million dollars? Not really.<br/>What would you do if you had a million dollars? Buy a car.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the Simple Past verb + <span class=\"italic\">would</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"IF\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Conditional\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"simple past \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"would + base verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I married Peter,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I would be happy.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"it snowed next July,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I would be very surprised.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I were you,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I would be jumping up and down.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Remember to use a comma (,) after the IF clause. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In conversation, it is common to use contractions. (I would = I'd).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If I were you, I'd be jumping up and down.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'd get that checked out if I were you.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If we went home, we'd need to have some movies to watch.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Giving Advice", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use modals to give advice. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The most common modals for giving advice are:<br/><span class=\"italic\"> should</span>, <span class=\"italic\">ought to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">had better</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can think of modals as \u201chelping verbs\u201d. They add meaning to the main verb of a sentence. In this case, these modals add the meaning of advice. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"> Should</span> is the most common modal used to give advice. <br/> <span class=\"italic\"> Ought to</span> and <span class=\"italic\"> had better</span>  are used for giving strong advice.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main Verb\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"should\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"get\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"moving.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"ought to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"go\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"home and relax.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"had better\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sit\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"down.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_backg